## Curated builds

Reviewed against patch 2.2.16 on 2026-10-01. The live patch is 2.2.16a, so these have not been re-read against it yet.

### Gold Lane Default (Gold)

- Items: Swift Boots, Haas's Claws, Berserker's Fury, Malefic Gun, Windtalker, Blade of Despair
- Core: Haas's Claws, Berserker's Fury, Malefic Gun
- Emblem: Assassin Emblem with Rupture, Master Assassin, Quantum Charge
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Flex: Sea Halberd over Windtalker when Use when healing or shielding erases your burst window, such as against Estes, Floryn, or sustain-heavy EXP lanes.; Wind of Nature over Blade of Despair when Use against physical dive threats like Ling or Hayabusa that can reach you before your frontline stabilizes. It does not block magic or True Damage.; Rose Gold Meteor over Blade of Despair when Use against magic burst that threatens to delete you in one spell cycle, such as from Eudora, Aurora, or Kadita.; Great Dragon Spear over Windtalker when Use when you are ahead and want Great Dragon Spear's movement speed to follow up Worldie's first-target slow while saving Slide for escape and a fresh Powerball.
- Total cost: 12130 gold

Standard crit-first ranked build. Worldie sets up a target at the edge of your attack range, while Malefic Gun supplies penetration now that the ultimate no longer reduces Physical Defense. Save Slide for repositioning and a fresh Powerball, with Flicker as a second escape.

### Anti-Tank Sustained (Gold)

- Items: Swift Boots, Haas's Claws, Berserker's Fury, Demon Hunter Sword, Malefic Gun, Windtalker
- Core: Haas's Claws, Berserker's Fury, Demon Hunter Sword
- Emblem: Marksman Emblem with Fatal, Weapon Master, Quantum Charge
- Battle spell: Inspire
- Flex: Sea Halberd over Demon Hunter Sword when Use when anti-heal is more urgent than percent-HP damage, such as against Estes, Floryn, or multiple lifesteal items on the enemy team.; Wind of Nature over Malefic Gun when Use when physical dive is the primary loss condition and you need the active immunity more than extra range.
- Total cost: 11300 gold

For HP-stacking frontlines when your team can peel and the enemy has little dive or poke. Demon Hunter Sword follows the crit pair. Use Inspire after enemy mobility is spent, and choose a Flicker build when you need another escape.

### Anti-Dive Survival (Gold)

- Items: Tough Boots, Haas's Claws, Berserker's Fury, Malefic Gun, Wind of Nature, Blade of Despair
- Core: Haas's Claws, Berserker's Fury, Malefic Gun
- Emblem: Assassin Emblem with Rupture, Master Assassin, Killing Spree
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Flex: Rose Gold Meteor over Wind of Nature when Use when magic burst is the primary threat instead of physical dive, such as against double-mage comps or a fed burst mage.; Swift Boots over Tough Boots when Use when the enemy draft has minimal crowd control and you can afford the greedier attack-speed boots.; Sea Halberd over Blade of Despair when Use when healing is the problem and you cannot afford to delay anti-heal, such as against a fed sustain fighter or Estes.
- Total cost: 12150 gold

Survival build against physical dive. Tough Boots shorten control chains and Wind of Nature blocks Physical Damage. Slide reloads a Powerball as you reposition, while Flicker covers a second escape. Killing Spree restores HP when you damage a low-HP hero and resets its cooldown on a kill.

